  "document": "k08-heading-is-a-link",
  "tests": "Section headings that are themselves hyperlinks, alongside an ordinary inline link in body text.",
  "attacks": "Element nesting. The correct structure is a heading CONTAINING a link. Tagging the link and losing the heading costs navigation; tagging the heading and losing the link costs the destination; emitting them as siblings duplicates the text. Also tests whether the version/reviewed line is mistaken for a subheading.",
